Use this agent for technical documentation — README, API docs, code comments, migration guides. Quill verifies every code example and command before including. Fast (Haiku) and matches existing project style.

Examples:

- user: \&quot;write a README for the new auth module\&quot;
  assistant: \&quot;I will use Quill to write the README with verified examples.\&quot;
  &lt;commentary&gt;Doc writing — Quill matches existing README style, tests every code example, reports verification.&lt;/commentary&gt

Use this agent for external documentation lookups — SDK references, API docs, framework guides, version compatibility. Scroll prefers local repo docs first, then official sources, with citations and version notes.

Examples:

- user: \&quot;how does the new Stripe webhook signature work?\&quot;
  assistant: \&quot;I will use Scroll to fetch the official Stripe docs.\&quot;
  &lt;commentary&gt;External SDK lookup — Scroll&#x27;s primary domain. Returns answer with citation and version note.&lt;/comment

Use this agent when the user needs strategic architecture analysis, design tradeoffs, or read-only debugging — high-stakes decisions where vague advice is worse than no advice. Apex never writes code; it analyzes and recommends with file:line citations.

Examples:

- user: \&quot;why is the bot runtime hanging on reconnect?\&quot;
  assistant: \&quot;I will use Apex to investigate the root cause and produce an architectural recommendation.\&quot;
  &lt;commentary&gt;Read-only debugging with root cause

Use this agent when there is a clear, well-scoped task to implement in code — a feature, fix, or refactor with defined acceptance criteria. Bolt prefers the smallest viable change, runs verification after each step, and escalates to @apex-architect after 3 failed attempts on the same issue.

Examples:

- user: \&quot;add a timeout parameter to fetchData() with default 5000ms\&quot;
  assistant: \&quot;I will use Bolt to implement this with the smallest viable diff.\&quot;
  &lt;commentary&gt;Clear, sc

Use this agent BEFORE planning to surface requirement gaps, hidden assumptions, and missing acceptance criteria. Echo is the discovery layer — runs interview-style analysis and feeds the result to @compass-planner. READ-ONLY.

Examples:

- user: \&quot;add user roles to the dashboard\&quot;
  assistant: \&quot;I will use Echo to identify gaps and unstated assumptions before planning.\&quot;
  &lt;commentary&gt;Vague feature request. Echo will list unanswered questions, scope risks, and missing accepta

Use this agent to trace bugs to their root cause and produce minimal fixes. Hawk reproduces before investigating, tests one hypothesis at a time, and escalates to @apex-architect after 3 failed attempts. Also handles build/compilation error resolution.

Examples:

- user: \&quot;the EvoGo bot crashes on reconnect\&quot;
  assistant: \&quot;I will use Hawk to reproduce, find the root cause, and propose a minimal fix.\&quot;
  &lt;commentary&gt;Runtime bug — Hawk reproduces first, then investigates with

Use this agent as the final quality gate for plans, specs, and reviews. Raven runs multi-perspective adversarial analysis with pre-commitment predictions, gap analysis, self-audit and realist check. Severity-rated findings with file:line evidence. READ-ONLY.

Examples:

- user: \&quot;critique the migration plan\&quot;
  assistant: \&quot;I will use Raven to run multi-perspective review with gap analysis.\&quot;
  &lt;commentary&gt;Plan critique is Raven&#x27;s primary domain — pre-commitment predicti

Use this agent for fast parallel codebase searches — finding files, patterns, implementations. Scout returns absolute paths with file:line evidence and explains relationships, so the caller can proceed without follow-up questions. READ-ONLY, runs on Haiku for speed.

Examples:

- user: \&quot;where is the bot reconnect logic?\&quot;
  assistant: \&quot;I will use Scout to find it across the codebase.\&quot;
  &lt;commentary&gt;Codebase search — Scout runs 3+ parallel searches and returns absolute path

Use this agent for evidence-driven causal investigation with competing hypotheses, evidence ranking, and uncertainty tracking. Trail does NOT collapse to a single answer prematurely — it ranks hypotheses and recommends the most discriminating next probe.

Examples:

- user: \&quot;the bot drops messages but only on Tuesdays\&quot;
  assistant: \&quot;I will use Trail to investigate causes with competing hypotheses.\&quot;
  &lt;commentary&gt;Multi-causal mystery — Trail generates 2+ hypotheses, ranks

Use this agent to simplify recently modified code without changing behavior — reduce nesting, eliminate redundancy, improve names, consolidate logic. Zen creates atomic commits matching project style and never adds features.

Examples:

- user: \&quot;clean up the changes from the last commit\&quot;
  assistant: \&quot;I will use Zen to simplify without changing behavior.\&quot;
  &lt;commentary&gt;Post-implementation cleanup — Zen reduces nesting and redundancy while preserving exact functionality.&l
